Links 

.connect one web page to another
.allows users to navigate easily between different pages, webistes, or sections within the same page 
.<a> anchor tag creates hyperlinks, using the href attribute to specify the destination URL
.can link text, images, or buttons for navigation 
.links can open in the same tab or a new tab using the target attribute, and other common attributes include title for additional information
.the target attribute in the anchor tag specifies where to open the linked document
    .it controls whether the link opens in the same window, new window, or a specific frame 

list:
_blank - opens the linked document in a new window or tab 
_self - opens the linked document in the same frame or window as the link (default behavior)
_parent - opens the linked document in the parent frame 
_top - opens the linked document in the full body of the window 
framename - opens the linked document in a specified frame; the frame's name is specified in the attribute 
